cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnthroSim in research, cite the released software version and preserve the exact source revision used for the experiment."
title: "AnthroSim"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Datengu"
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: 2026-08-29
repository-code: "https://github.com/Datengu/anthrosim"
url: "https://github.com/Datengu/anthrosim"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - agent-based simulation
  - anthropology
  - archaeology
  - reproducibility
  - demography
  - migration
  - temporary mobility
  - aggregation
  - sensitivity analysis
  - identifiability
abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained permanent household migration,
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments, and explicit temporary mobility and
  aggregation under declared model assumptions. Version 0.3.1 is a post-v0.3.0
  audit and research-readiness hardening release. It preserves the M9 capability
  baseline while strengthening scientific configuration/provenance, stochastic
  precision, long-run diagnostics, demographic-baseline interpretation, and
  identifiability/equifinality safeguards for calibration and competing-hypothesis
  analysis. AnthroSim is not an empirically validated model of human prehistory.
